# Security Controls

Purpose:
  Security control specifications for the SDDRA system.

Owns: security\controls.sdd
Spec: SecurityControls

Controls:

  SEC.SECRET:
    detect exposed secrets
    scan: truffleHog, gitleaks, detect-secrets
    scope: source code, config, environment

  SEC.DEP:
    detect vulnerable dependencies
    scan: npm audit, snyk, osv-scanner, grype
    scope: package.json, go.mod, requirements.txt

  SEC.SAST:
    static code security analysis
    scan: semgrep, bandit, eslint-plugin-security, gosec
    scope: source code

  SEC.DAST:
    runtime application security testing
    scan: owasp-zap, burp, nuclei
    scope: running application

  SEC.AUTH:
    authentication/authorization validation
    scan: custom tests, OWASP ASVS
    scope: auth flows, session management

  SEC.INPUT:
    input validation
    scan: custom tests, fuzzing
    scope: API endpoints, forms, file uploads

  SEC.RATE:
    rate limiting
    scan: custom tests, load testing
    scope: API endpoints, public resources

  SEC.AUDIT:
    security-sensitive audit logging
    scan: custom tests, log review
    scope: auth, payment, admin actions

  SEC.THREAT:
    threat model review
    scan: manual review, PASTA, STRIDE
    scope: architecture, data flow, trust boundaries

  SEC.PENTEST:
    penetration testing
    scan: manual pentest, automated tools
    scope: public-facing components, auth, payment

  SEC.CONTAINER:
    container/image security
    scan: trivy, anchore, docker scout
    scope: Dockerfile, base images, runtime

  SEC.SUPPLY:
    software supply-chain security
    scan: sigstore, slsa, dependency review
    scope: build pipeline, dependencies, artifacts

  SEC.DDOS:
    DDoS readiness
    scan: load testing, architecture review
    scope: public endpoints, CDN, WAF, autoscaling

  SEC.BUSINESS:
    business logic security
    scan: custom tests, BDD security scenarios
    scope: payment, refund, auth, admin

RuntimePatternSet:
    definition: 17 regex patterns seeded from claude-code patterns.py:30-345
    source: anthropics/claude-code plugins/security-guidance/hooks/patterns.py:30-345
    execution: claude-code PostToolUse[Edit/Write] hook via adapter-runtime.sdd
    best_practices_ref: tmp/web-research/best-practices-findings.md#key-findings-3-4-6-9
    reachability_classification:
      reachable_critical: Block immediately (exit 2)
      reachable_high: Block (exit 2)
      reachable_medium: Warn + ticket
      unreachable_any: Log only (no block)

    patterns:
      PAT.yaml_load:
        regex: yaml\.load\s*\(
        description: Unsafe YAML deserialization (RCE)
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous if loading untrusted YAML at runtime
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use yaml.safe_load() instead

      PAT.pickle_loads:
        regex: pickle\.(loads|load)\s*\(
        description: Unsafe pickle deserialization (RCE)
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous with untrusted serialized data
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use JSON or struct for serialization

      PAT.eval_exec:
        regex: \b(eval|exec)\s*\(
        description: Arbitrary code execution
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — direct code execution risk
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Avoid eval/exec; use ast.literal_eval or sandboxed alternatives

      PAT.shell_true:
        regex: shell\s*=\s*True
        description: Shell command injection risk via subprocess
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous with user-controlled input
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use shell=False with argument list

      PAT.innerHTML:
        regex: (innerHTML|dangerouslySetInnerHTML)
        description: XSS via unsafe HTML injection (React)
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L2
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous with untrusted content
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use DOMPurify or text content instead

      PAT_sql_concat:
        regex: (['"]\s*\+\s*sql|['"]\s*\+\s*query|['"]\s*f['"].*SELECT)
        description: SQL injection via string concatenation
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous with user input reaching query
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use parameterized queries / prepared statements

      PAT_hardcoded_secret:
        regex: (api[_-]?key|secret|password|token|passwd)\s*[:=]\s*[a-zA-Z0-9'"]{8,}
        description: Hardcoded secret in source
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: always — secrets in source are always exploitable
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use environment variables / vault / secrets manager

      PAT_weak_random:
        regex: random\.(random|uniform|randint|choice)
        description: Weak randomness (not for security/cryptography)
        severity: MEDIUM
        L_level: L2
        reachability: context-dependent — dangerous only for security tokens
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use secrets module for security-sensitive randomness

      PAT_weak_crypto:
        regex: hashlib\.(md5|sha1)\s*\(
        description: Weak hash algorithm (MD5/SHA1)
        severity: MEDIUM
        L_level: L2
        reachability: runtime — dangerous for password hashing, signatures
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Use SHA-256 or stronger

      PAT_path_traversal:
        regex: (open\(|readFile|writeFile)\s*[^)]*(\.|..)*[/\\]
        description: Potential path traversal
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous with user-controlled paths
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Validate and canonicalize file paths; use safe join

      PAT_cors_wildcard:
        regex: Access-Control-Allow-Origin\s*:\s*['"]?\*['"]?
        description: CORS wildcard allows all origins
        severity: MEDIUM
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — exploitable if API serves sensitive data
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Restrict to specific trusted origins

      PAT_missing_auth:
        regex: (def\s+(login|auth|admin)\w*\s*[:\(])|(app\.(post|get)\s*\(*['"](/admin|/api))
        description: Missing authentication/authorization check
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — directly exploitable
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time + staging_time
        fix: Add auth middleware and authorization checks

      PAT_ssrf:
        regex: (fetch\(|requests\.(get|post|put|delete))\s*\(.*(\+|f['"]|concat|format)
        description: Potential SSRF via user-controlled URL
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous if URL reaches internal network
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time + staging_time
        fix: Validate and allowlist URL schemas/hosts

      PAT_open_redirect:
        regex: redirect\s*\(.*request\.
        description: Open redirect via user-controlled URL
        severity: MEDIUM
        L_level: L2
        reachability: runtime — exploitable for phishing campaigns
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Validate redirect targets against allowlist

      PAT_deserialize_untrusted:
        regex: (pickle|yaml\.load|marshal\.load)\s*\(\s*request\.
        description: Deserialization of untrusted user input
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — directly exploitable
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Never deserialize untrusted input; use JSON/Protocol Buffers

      PAT_redos:
        regex: (\([a-zA-Z+\*]*\*\?)|(\(\.\*\)\{.*,.\\})
        description: Potential regex denial of service (ReDoS)
        severity: LOW
        L_level: L1
        reachability: runtime — only dangerous with user-controlled regex input
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time
        fix: Avoid nested quantifiers in regex patterns

      PAT_no_rate_limit:
        regex: (def\s+login|app\.post\s*\(['"](/login|/api))
        description: Missing rate limiting on auth/API endpoints
        severity: LOW
        L_level: L1
        reachability: runtime — exploitable via brute force / DoS
        sdlt_stage: build_time + pr_time + staging_time
        fix: Add rate limiting middleware (e.g., express-rate-limit)

      PAT_ai_missing_auth:
        description: AI-generated auth routes without explicit authorization checks
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — directly exploitable if deployed
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        best_practices_ref: tmp/web-research/best-practices-findings.md#key-finding-9
        rule: AI-generated code touching auth MUST have human review
        fix: Add explicit auth middleware and authorization checks

      PAT_ai_hardcoded_credential:
        description: AI autocomplete inserting API keys or tokens
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: always — secrets in source are always exploitable
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use environment variables / vault / secrets manager

      PAT_ai_eval_usage:
        description: AI-generated eval/exec for dynamic code execution
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — direct code execution risk
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Avoid eval/exec; use ast.literal_eval or sandboxed alternatives

      PAT_ai_shell_true:
        description: AI-generated subprocess calls with shell=True
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime — dangerous with user-controlled input
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use shell=False with argument list

      PAT_ai_yaml_load:
        description: AI-generated yaml.load instead of yaml.safe_load
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime — dangerous if loading untrusted YAML
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use yaml.safe_load() instead

SkillPatternSets:
  purpose: Language-specific security patterns activated only when the corresponding programming language skill is in use
  selection: Inferred from file_path extension in hook payload; merged with base RuntimePatternSet
  execution: sdd-adapter/hook-bridge.ts selects active skill set; patterns-runtime.ts scans with merged set

  languages/go:
    skill_id: languages/go
    file_extensions:
      - .go
    patterns:
      PAT.go_exec_inject:
        regex: exec\.Command\s*\(.*\+
        description: Go exec.Command with string concatenation (command injection)
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L4
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use argument list; never concatenate user input into command

      PAT.go_template_xss:
        regex: template\.HTML\s*\(
        description: Go template.HTML allows raw HTML injection (XSS)
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use template.HTML only with sanitized content; prefer text/template

      PAT.go_sql_concat:
        regex: (db\.Query|db\.Exec|sql\.Raw)\s*\(.*\+
        description: Go SQL query with string concatenation
        severity: CRITICAL
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use parameterized queries / prepared statements

      PAT.go_weak_crypto:
        regex: (md5|sha1)\.New\(\)
        description: Go weak hash algorithm (MD5/SHA1)
        severity: MEDIUM
        L_level: L2
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use SHA-256 or stronger via crypto/sha256

      PAT.go_insecure_http:
        regex: http\.(Get|Post|Do)\s*\(.*\+.*\)
        description: Go HTTP request with user-controlled URL
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Validate and allowlist URL schemes/hosts

  languages/python:
    skill_id: languages/python
    file_extensions:
      - .py
    patterns:
      PAT.py_os_system:
        regex: os\.system\s*\(
        description: os.system() allows shell injection
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use subprocess.run with shell=False and argument list

      PAT.py_subprocess_popen:
        regex: subprocess\.(call|run|Popen)\s*\(.*shell\s*=\s*True
        description: subprocess with shell=True enables command injection
        severity: HIGH
        L_level: L3
        reachability: runtime
        sdlt_stage: pr_time + build_time
        fix: Use shell=False with explicit argument list

Enforcement:
        best_practices_ref: tmp/web-research/best-practices-findings.md#key-finding-3
        diff_aware_gating:
          rule: Only block on findings introduced by the change under review
          rule: Track pre-existing findings as scheduled remediation, not merge blockers
        gate_actions:
          reachable_critical: BLOCK (exit 2)
          reachable_high: BLOCK (exit 2)
          reachable_medium: WARN + ticket
          unreachable_critical: WARN + ticket
          unreachable_any: LOG only (no block)
          kev_listed: BLOCK if reachable
        mode_observe: L0-L3 patterns below project threshold — warn only (OBS12)
        mode_enforce: L4-L5 patterns at or above threshold — block (OBS13, exit 2)
        source: .sdd/runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd (HookBridge)
        source: .sdd/gates/security-enforcement.sdd (EnforcementModel)
        rule: Block on findings that are BOTH reachable AND exploitable
        rule: Warn + ticket on reachable-but-not-exploitable findings
        rule: Log-only for unreachable findings (no merge block)

SEC.PINJECT:
  detect prompt injection in user-supplied prompts
  scan: PromptGuard (sdd-adapter/security/prompt-guard.ts)
  scope: all user input before command dispatch and hook processing
  patterns: PI-001 through PI-010 (see security/prompt-injection.sdd)
  response_modes:
    BLOCK: exit 2, halt execution, audit payload hash
    WARN: exit 0, proceed with warning, emit OBS15
    LOG: exit 0, log finding, proceed normally
  severity_decision:
    any_CRITICAL: BLOCK
    2+ HIGH: BLOCK
    1 HIGH: WARN
    MEDIUM/LOW only: LOG
    none: PASS
  integration:
    hook-bridge: guard on UserPromptSubmit (OBS14 on BLOCK)
    commands: guard customerPrompt before dispatch (OBS14 on BLOCK)
  whitelist: project-scoped, time-bounded (expires required)
  best_practices_ref: .sdd/security/prompt-injection.sdd

ControlSelection:
  Controls are selected based on:
    SecurityLevel (L0-L5)
    Task risk (R0-R5)
    Affected layers
    Data sensitivity
    External exposure

  Mandatory controls (all projects):
    SEC.SECRET
    SEC.DEP
    SEC.SAST
    SEC.PINJECT

  Conditional controls (based on risk/level):
    R2+ ? SEC.SAST, SEC.DEP, SEC.AUTH
    R3+ ? SEC.THREAT, SEC.DAST
    R4+ ? SEC.PENTEST, SEC.AUDIT
    L3+ ? SEC.DAST, SEC.THREAT
    L4+ ? SEC.PENTEST
    L5+ ? SEC.SUPPLY, SEC.CONTAINER, external assessment

State: +
  Note:
  This file is the security controls
  catalog. Each control has a unique ID, purpose, scan tools, and
  scope. Controls are selected based on SecurityLevel and task risk,
  not applied uniformly.
